 ## OL-1b manifest-declared Organization ledger locus — 2026-10-09
 
-Owner: `ORGANIZATION-BATCH-CUSTODY-REPLAY-001` (Q-OL6: one owner for `ledger_store.py` and `organization_store()`). Approved in StegVerse-Labs/TVC#488 (ChatGPT FINAL review, comment 6084480922, answering comment 6084332899). The Organization ledger locus is declared by the Organization manifest, not chosen by the host. `.stegverse/transition-ledger/org-contract.json` declares `organization_ledger` = `{"store":"git","ref":"refs/heads/organization-ledger/StegVerse-Labs","custody":"PRIVATE","propagate_target":null}` (the ref is in G1-R's `GitLedgerStore` namespace and passes its ref validation). `resident-runtime/aggregate_repo_transition.py::organization_store()` reads that declaration first. `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_STORE`, `_GIT_REF`, `_GIT_REMOTE` and `_GIT_CUSTODY` are non-authoritative: each one present must equal the declared value, otherwise the append is refused FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_LOCUS_MISMATCH` before any store is built, so nothing is appended. A missing or malformed declaration is FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_LOCUS_NOT_DECLARED`; there is no environment-only fallback and no silent POSIX default. The POSIX store is selected only by an explicit `{"store":"posix"}` declaration (the test suite declares it in `tests/conftest.py`, and in child interpreters through `tests/posix_ledger_locus/`). `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_GIT_DIR` (and `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_ROOT` for a declared POSIX store) stays host-supplied, because it is the local materialization path and not the destination. `propagate` reaches only the declared `propagate_target`, and only when that target is declared with `custody: PRIVATE`. With the approved `null`, the store has no remote and `GitLedgerStore.propagate` returns its existing typed non-gating FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_REMOTE_NOT_SUPPLIED`, while the local compare-and-swap append completes and the chain continues. A caller that already holds a store or root still passes it directly, as before.
+Owner: `ORGANIZATION-BATCH-CUSTODY-REPLAY-001` (Q-OL6: one owner for `ledger_store.py` and `organization_store()`). Approved in StegVerse-Labs/TVC#488 (ChatGPT FINAL review, comment 6084480922, answering comment 6084332899). The Organization ledger locus is declared by the Organization manifest, not chosen by the host. `.stegverse/transition-ledger/org-contract.json` declares `organization_ledger` = `{"store":"git","ref":"refs/stegverse/organization-ledger","custody":"PRIVATE","propagate_target":{"custody":"PRIVATE","remote":"https://github.com/StegVerse-Labs/.github"}}`: the owner designated the location structure StegVerse-org/.github uses (its organization ledger on its own `refs/stegverse/organization-ledger`), relayed on StegVerse-org/StegVerse-SDK#465 for #3099. That ref is admitted by `GitLedgerStore` as `DESIGNATED_LEDGER_REF` alongside its `refs/heads/organization-ledger/` namespace; the earlier `refs/heads/organization-ledger/StegVerse-Labs` with a `null` target was approved in TVC#488 and was never published. `resident-runtime/aggregate_repo_transition.py::organization_store()` reads that declaration first. `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_STORE`, `_GIT_REF`, `_GIT_REMOTE` and `_GIT_CUSTODY` are non-authoritative: each one present must equal the declared value, otherwise the append is refused FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_LOCUS_MISMATCH` before any store is built, so nothing is appended. A missing or malformed declaration is FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_LOCUS_NOT_DECLARED`; there is no environment-only fallback and no silent POSIX default. The POSIX store is selected only by an explicit `{"store":"posix"}` declaration (the test suite declares it in `tests/conftest.py`, and in child interpreters through `tests/posix_ledger_locus/`). `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_GIT_DIR` (and `STEGVERSE_ORG_LEDGER_ROOT` for a declared POSIX store) stays host-supplied, because it is the local materialization path and not the destination. `propagate` reaches only the declared `propagate_target`, and only when that target is declared with `custody: PRIVATE`. With a `null` target the store has no remote and `GitLedgerStore.propagate` returns its existing typed non-gating FAIL_CLOSED `ORGANIZATION_LEDGER_REMOTE_NOT_SUPPLIED`, while the local compare-and-swap append completes and the chain continues. The governance decision workflow materializes the designated ref before its cycle, publishes it fast-forward only after the mesh, and reads it back from a fresh fetch. A caller that already holds a store or root still passes it directly, as before.
 
 **Evidence class: SOURCE_IMPLEMENTED, local test results only** (temporary bare repositories and POSIX roots). No real ledger ref was created, no propagation target was named, and no runtime ALLOW is claimed. `ledger_store.py` semantics are unchanged; there is no new dependency, workflow, service, store, scheduler or framework.
 
